From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: setup asks how NickelOS should work

The first time NickelOS starts, before the first account is made, setup
asks how NickelOS should work (docs/setup-experiences.md in
overlay-nickel):

- Privacy, preselected: DuckDuckGo is the search engine for the browser and
  the launcher.
- Google: Google is.
- Minimal: the launcher searches only the device (its web results are off);
  the browser's search engine is left to the user.

The screen is nickel-setup (NickelSetupScreen, NickelSetupScreenHandler,
nickel-setup-element), text only, with ChromeOS's card radio buttons as on
the theme screen; its strings are in ui_chromeos_strings.grd. The wizard
shows it in place of local-account-creation while the device has no
accounts; it skips itself once one exists.

The choice waits in the local state pref nickel.setup.pending_experience
until the new account first signs in. NickelOS restarts Chrome as the
account's Linux user then, so the session's own OOBE screens never run:
UserSessionManager::PerformPostBrowserLaunchOOBEActions applies it
(NickelSetupScreen::MaybeApplyChoice) and keeps it in the profile pref
nickel.setup.experience (ash/constants/nickel_pref_names.h) for what comes
next, the apps each experience suggests.

